# Bounded operative-pattern waivers, read by test/operative-move-detector.test.js.
#
# Format:  OP-WAIVER: <skill-path> <pattern> -<max-drop> — <reason>
#
# Bounded on all three axes: one skill, one pattern, one maximum magnitude. A
# drop LARGER than the declared number still fails. This is deliberately not a
# blanket switch, and it is deliberately committed: a waiver belongs in git
# history next to the change that needed it, where it can be read, blamed, and
# removed when the reason expires.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS INSTEAD OF A WIDER REGEX:
# The first attempt at these two entries broadened countPatterns.step_headings
# to also count bolded ordered-list items. That looked tidier and was far worse:
# measured across 106 skills it granted ~400 units of undetectable deletion
# budget to buy the 12 units needed here, and it let a "1. **name**: ..."
# companion-skills list satisfy a gate meant to protect an ordered procedure.
# Deleting all four real "### Phase N" headings from systematic-debugging passed
# under it. Two narrow, reviewable waivers are the correct trade.
#
# Before adding an entry: prefer restoring the content, or moving it into the
# skill's reference.md where the loader can still reach it. Waive only a genuine
# re-encoding where the operative content demonstrably survives.

# PHR's seven "### Step 0..6" headings became an eight-item numbered procedure
# under "## Review process" (skill.md). Every step survives -- fresh-reader
# check, dispatch, score, veto, verdict, remediate, correlation, convergence --
# and the resident kernel still carries the veto and convergence rules. The
# encoding changed; the procedure did not.
OP-WAIVER: engineering/progressive-harsh-review/skill.md step_headings -7 — kernel split re-encoded "### Step N" as a numbered procedure list; all steps retained

# context-ferry's five "### Step N" headings likewise became a numbered list;
# the output path, PreCompact abbreviated path, and fidelity handling all remain
# resident, with the full template in reference.md.
OP-WAIVER: productivity/context-ferry/skill.md step_headings -5 — kernel split re-encoded "### Step N" as a numbered procedure list; all steps retained

# debate's five "### Step N" headings and five stop markers live in
# reference.md, which its loader resolves (source checkout, installed sp-debate
# alias, and all three install roots -- exercised by 15 cases in
# tests/engineering/debate-safety.bats). Content moved, not deleted.
OP-WAIVER: engineering/debate/skill.md step_headings -5 — moved to reachable reference.md; loader coverage in debate-safety.bats
OP-WAIVER: engineering/debate/skill.md stop_markers -5 — moved to reachable reference.md; loader coverage in debate-safety.bats

# context-ferry's output-path and confirmation fences now live under
# "## Output path" in reference.md; the path itself remains resident at
# skill.md's numbered step 5, so the instruction never left the kernel.
OP-WAIVER: productivity/context-ferry/skill.md code_fences -3 — output-scaffold fences moved to reachable reference.md; path stays resident
